Surfaces Joustur Skatur as a coming-soon mode inside Punch Skater across the sk8rpunk.com hub, and eliminates the dead-end for any `?page=joustur-skatur` landing.

## Changes

### `src/App.tsx`

- **Punch Skater tile** — added `"Joustur Skatur (soon)"` to the feature chip list so the upcoming mode is visible on the live game card.

- **Joustur Skatur teaser section** — new `<section>` inserted between the Games hub and Character Bios. Frames the mode as an async street-ritual board-game inside Punch Skater (Royal Game of Ur lineage), uses on-brand copy, and closes with a `Play Punch Skater ↗` CTA styled with the existing cyan accent.

- **`?page=joustur-skatur` redirect** — follows the existing `?page=bios` routing pattern; calls `window.location.replace(punchskaterUrl)` so the route sends users directly to Punch Skater instead of 404-ing or dead-ending.

```tsx
if (page === "joustur-skatur") {
  window.location.replace(punchskaterUrl);
  return null;
}
```

With `options.create === 0` (default), new tabs opened in rapid succession would frequently fail to move next to the active tab due to a race condition in the `onCreated` handler.

## Root Cause

The handler awaited several async operations before calling `getTabs()` to check if the new tab was at the far right:

```javascript
var tabs = await getTabs(tab.windowId);
if (tab.index === tabs.length - 1) { // broken: tabs.length includes tabs created during the awaits
  await chrome.tabs.move(tab.id, { index: selIndex + 1 });
}
```

If another tab was created during those awaits, `getTabs()` would return a longer list — making `tabs.length - 1 > tab.index` and silently skipping the move.

## Fix

Replace the async `getTabs()` call with a comparison against the already-fetched `cachedTabs.length`, which captures the pre-existing tab count before this new tab was added:

```javascript
if (tab.index >= cachedTabs.length) {
  await chrome.tabs.move(tab.id, { index: selIndex + 1 });
}
```

This eliminates the extra async round-trip and makes the far-right check race-free.

